== Foundation Models for Segmentation

SAM's modular design, a frozen ViT encoder paired with a lightweight mask decoder and a flexible prompt interface, has spawned a family of derivative models that collectively validate the architectural assumptions underlying our approach. Several works improve SAM without modifying the encoder. SAM-HQ @ke2023samhq introduces a learnable high-quality output token that refines boundary predictions inside the decoder, demonstrating that meaningful quality gains are achievable while leaving the encoder frozen. EfficientSAM @xiong2024efficientsam distills SAM's ViT-H into ViT-Tiny and ViT-Small backbones via SAMI masked-image pretraining, showing that SAM's feature space is sufficiently well-structured to survive aggressive compression. MobileSAM @zhang2023mobilesam takes a complementary route through decoupled knowledge distillation into a TinyViT encoder that is 60 times smaller, further confirming that the decoder module functions independently of encoder scale. FastSAM @zhao2023fastsam replaces the transformer encoder entirely with a YOLOv8-seg CNN backbone, achieving a 50-fold speedup at the cost of some accuracy. These efficiency-oriented works reinforce a central premise of our method. Because the encoder can be frozen, compressed, or even swapped, a learned prompt policy operating through the prompt interface is architecture-agnostic and forward-compatible with future SAM variants.

A parallel line of research explores alternative prompting paradigms that depart from SAM's point-and-box interface. SegGPT @wang2023seggpt frames segmentation as in-context learning through masked image modeling, where visual examples replace spatial prompts altogether. SEEM @zou2023seem unifies clicks, boxes, text, and referring regions into a single multi-modal prompt composition framework, broadening the space of possible user intents. Grounding DINO @liu2024groundingdino provides open-set, text-driven object detection that identifies _what_ to segment, while Grounded-SAM @ren2024groundedsam assembles Grounding DINO with SAM to achieve end-to-end text-to-mask generation, validating SAM's role as a composable segmentation module. Semantic-SAM @li2024semanticsam addresses granularity ambiguity by producing multi-granularity masks with semantic labels from a single click, highlighting a limitation our decomposition strategy also targets. Collectively, these models demonstrate that SAM's prompt interface is the natural control surface for downstream systems. Our work exploits this insight by treating prompt placement itself as a learnable policy, rather than requiring architectural modifications or end-to-end retraining.
